  "content": {
    "id": "p43-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "If $y=px^2+(p+1)x+\\dfrac{p}{4}$, find the values of $p$ such that the parabola is always below the $x$-axis.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$p<-\\dfrac12$.",
      "worked": "The parabola must be concave down and have no $x$-intercepts, so $p<0$ and $\\Delta<0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(p+1)^2-4p\\left(\\frac p4\\right)\\\\\\Delta&=p^2+2p+1-p^2\\\\\\Delta&=2p+1\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}2p+1&<0\\\\p&<-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nThese values also satisfy $p<0$, so the parabola is always below the $x$-axis.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
